---
kind: lore
id: camp.talks
title: Camp conversations
components: [../components/reaction.component.lute, ../components/idle.component.lute]
---
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- Isolde */

<beat id="isoldeSold" on="talk" target="npc.isolde" title="Isolde, after the sale" priority="40" when="run.bridge == 'sold' && holds('inParty', ['isolde'])">
  @isolde{code="0010" emotion="angry"}: Don't. Whatever you are about to say, don't.
  @isolde{code="0020"}: I have been the sword that did the Company's sums before. I know what it feels like from the inside. I didn't think I'd have to learn what it looks like from next to you.
</beat>

<beat id="isoldeRoll" on="talk" target="npc.isolde" title="The Coldwater roll" priority="30" when="holds('knows', ['roll']) && holds('inParty', ['isolde'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: You hand Isolde the tin box. She reads the roll standing up, and then she sits down on the wagon step and reads it again.
  @isolde{code="0010" emotion="sad"}: Hesketh. The miller. He gave us water. I did not know his name until now.
  @isolde{code="0020"}: Thank you. I think. Ask me tomorrow.
  ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="adores" instance="use-001"}
</beat>

<beat id="isoldeOath" on="talk" target="npc.isolde" title="Isolde's oath" priority="20" when="holds('inParty', ['isolde']) && run.approval.isolde >= 2 && quest.isoldeOath.state == 'unset'">
  @isolde{code="0010"}: May I tell you something I have not told Brannoc?
  @isolde{code="0020"}: I was at Coldwater. Company colours, Company horse. We were told it was a plague village. It wasn't. I rode out before the torches, and I have been riding out ever since.
  @isolde{code="0030"}: I swore that the next time, I would stay and stand in the way. I would like someone to hold me to it.
  <branch id="oath" prompt="Isolde is waiting.">
    <choice id="hold" label="\"I'll hold you to it. And you hold me.\"">
      ::accept{quest="isoldeOath"}
      ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="approves" instance="use-002"}
      @isolde{code="0040" emotion="content"}: Then that's two of us. It's a start.
    </choice>
    <choice id="past" label="Coldwater was years ago. Let it go.">
      ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="disapproves" instance="use-003"}
      @isolde{code="0050"}: The people of Coldwater would find that easier if they were alive to try.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<beat use="idle" id="isoldeIdle" who="isolde" instance="use-001">
  <match on="run.approval.isolde">
    <when is="3..">
      @isolde{code="0010" emotion="content"}: Sit. The fire's better on this side. So is the company.
    </when>
    <when is="..-1">
      @isolde{code="0020"}: Warden.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @isolde{code="0030"}: The sentries are posted. You should sleep while the road lets you.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- Corvin */

<beat id="corvinScheme" on="talk" target="npc.corvin" title="Corvin has an idea" priority="20" after="visited('bridge.arrival')" when="holds('inParty', ['corvin']) && run.bridge == 'held' && quest.toll.state == 'unset'">
  @corvin{code="0010"}: Hypothetically. If a person knew where three of Maelis's deserters were sleeping, and a sack of her silver with them.
  @corvin{code="0020"}: And hypothetically that person had helped them get there, for a fee, some months ago.
  @corvin{code="0030"}: Then that person would be sitting on the price of a bridge. Hypothetically.
  <branch id="scheme" prompt="Corvin is picking his teeth with a knife and not looking at you.">
    <choice id="listen" label="Go on. Hypothetically.">
      ::accept{quest="toll"}
      ::use{component="reaction" who="corvin" feel="approves" instance="use-004"}
      @corvin{code="0040"}: I'll do the talking when we see her. You do the nodding. You're good at nodding.
    </choice>
    <choice id="refuse" label="They're under Marrow roofs. No.">
      ::use{component="reaction" who="corvin" feel="disapproves" instance="use-005"}
      @corvin{code="0050"}: Noble. Expensive, but noble.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<beat use="idle" id="corvinIdle" who="corvin" instance="use-002">
  <match on="run.approval.corvin">
    <when is="3..">
      @corvin{code="0010"}: You know, Warden, I'm starting to think you might be worth the trouble.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @corvin{code="0020"}: If you're looking for honest advice, you've come to the wrong fire.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- Wren */

<beat id="wrenBrother" on="talk" target="npc.wren" title="What the river told Wren" priority="20" when="quest.wrenRoots.state == 'active' && @wrenWithUs">
  @wren{code="0010"}: You want to know how the river talks to me. It doesn't, mostly. It talked to Tam.
  @wren{code="0020"}: My brother. Deserted the Duskbound in spring. Maelis sent men to the ford after him, and the river took him before they could.
  @narrator{code="0010"}: She opens her hand. A flat grey stone, a hole worn through it, on a knotted string.
  @wren{code="0030"}: His token. He wanted to see the far side of the gorge. He never did.
  ::pickup{item="token"}
  ::set{run.approval.wren += 1}
</beat>

<beat use="idle" id="wrenIdle" who="wren" instance="use-003">
  <match on="run.approval.wren">
    <when is="2..">
      @wren{code="0010"}: The water's calm tonight. So am I. Don't get used to it.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @wren{code="0020"}: I'm listening to the river. You could try it. You'd hear less of yourself.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- any companion */
/* Walking up to a companion who has left the party (a kind target over the
member, dsl 0.27 §3: `departed` asked of `occasion.target`). The fallen are
out of reach altogether: the engine does not raise `talk` for them. */
<beat id="companionGone" on="talk" target="kind:companion" title="Gone" once="false" priority="-10" when="holds('departed', [occasion.target])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: {{occasion.target}}'s bedroll is gone from the wagon. So is {{occasion.target}}.
</beat>
/* Each night, every companion who trusts the Warden takes a turn at the watch
unasked (`for`, dsl 0.27 §3: once per member, on the untargeted camp). */
<beat id="watch" on="camp" for="kind:companion" title="The watch" once="false" priority="10" when="holds('loyal', [occasion.target])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: {{occasion.target}} takes a turn at the watch without being asked.
</beat>
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ford and the Company */

<beat id="odaThanks" on="talk" target="npc.oda" title="Oda" priority="10" when="run.hostagesFreed">
  @oda{code="0010"}: They're asleep. Both of them. In one bed, because neither will let go of the other.
  @oda{code="0020"}: I have nothing to give you but the thirty silver, and you have that. So have this: the Marrow folk will remember whose wagons came.
</beat>

<beat id="odaWaiting" on="talk" target="npc.oda" title="Oda" once="false">
  <match on="quest.hostages.state">
    <when is="active">
      @oda{code="0010"}: The mill. The Duskbound came and went by the mill. I'd swear to it.
    </when>
    <when is="failed">
      @oda{code="0020"}: Get out of my house.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @oda{code="0030"}: Company wagons. Company manners. Go away.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>

<beat id="brannocLedger" on="talk" target="npc.brannoc" title="Brannoc and the ledger" priority="10" when="holds('knows', ['ledger']) && run.bridge == 'held'">
  @brannoc{code="0010" emotion="angry"}: Someone's been in the ninth wagon. The seal's cut clean, which means it wasn't the mules.
  @brannoc{code="0020"}: Whatever you think you read, Warden, it's Company property. Put it back and we'll call it an accounting error.
  ::set{run.rep.company -= 1}
</beat>

<beat id="brannocIdle" on="talk" target="npc.brannoc" title="Brannoc" once="false">
  @brannoc{code="0010"}: Eleven wagons, Warden. I count them every night. You should too.
</beat>
